<h2>What you see</h2>

<p>Each view is a section through a room with an outside wall and a window. You change a few inputs and watch how the picture shifts in the model.</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Air in the room.</strong> A radiator below the window. Colors show warmer and cooler air in broad steps, on a fixed °C scale; markers show how the air moves. You choose the window, the wall, the radiator setting, the outside temperature, the room size and a curtain or a sofa in front of the window.</li>
    <li><strong>Cool walls and mould.</strong> The temperature of the inner wall surface and a risk estimate in three levels, with a range, for the flat wall and, in one line, for the outside edge. You choose the outdoor temperature, the humidity in the room and the wall. A real room corner is usually colder than this edge.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How it is calculated</h2>

<p>The wall is calculated with steady heat conduction from common design values; the air is a 2D flow simulation, shown qualitatively. The details are on the <a href="/method/">method</a> page, short answers under <a href="/faq/">questions and answers</a>.</p>

<p class="notice">If you can see mould: have the wall looked at on site by a professional.</p>

